---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Docs — Pageforge Programmatic SEO Generator"
  description="How to add CSV rows, generate landing pages, and deploy Pageforge to Netlify for free."
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 3rem;">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 760px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
      <h1 class="section-title" style="max-width: 14ch;">Ship pages from a spreadsheet</h1>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Pageforge is an Astro static site generator. Edit CSV → build → Netlify CDN. No runtime database.
      </p>

      <h2 id="quickstart" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.6rem;">Quickstart</h2>
      <pre class="code-panel"><code>npm install
npm run dev
<span class="comment"># open http://localhost:4321</span></code></pre>

      <h2 id="data" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.6rem;">1. Add rows to the dataset</h2>
      <p>
        Edit <code>data/pages.csv</code>. Each row becomes one landing page at
        <code>/pages/&lt;slug&gt;/</code>.
      </p>
      <pre class="code-panel"><code>slug,city,state,service,headline,subheadline,...
best-seo-agency-miami,Miami,FL,SEO Agency,Best SEO Agency in Miami,...</code></pre>

      <h2 id="templates" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.6rem;">2. Template + AI layer</h2>
      <p>
        The page template lives in <code>src/pages/pages/[slug].astro</code>. It injects:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>City/service-specific copy from the CSV</li>
        <li>LocalBusiness, Breadcrumb, and FAQ JSON-LD schema</li>
        <li>Internal links to related city and service pages</li>
        <li>Open Graph + canonical meta tags</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="build" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.6rem;">3. Build statically</h2>
      <pre class="code-panel"><code>npm run build
<span class="comment"># output → dist/</span></code></pre>

      <h2 id="deploy" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.6rem;">4. Deploy on Netlify ($0)</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Push this repo to GitHub.</li>
        <li>In Netlify: <strong>Add new site → Import an existing project</strong>.</li>
        <li>Build command: <code>npm run build</code></li>
        <li>Publish directory: <code>dist</code></li>
        <li>Deploy — every git push rebuilds and republishes automatically.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <code>netlify.toml</code> is already configured. Netlify’s free tier includes global CDN,
        HTTPS, and continuous deployment.
      </p>

      <pre class="code-panel"><code><span class="comment"># Optional: Netlify CLI</span>
npx netlify login
npx netlify init
npx netlify deploy --prod</code></pre>

      <h2 id="automation" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.6rem;">Automation loop</h2>
      <p>
        Update CSV → commit to GitHub → Netlify build hook fires → new pages go live worldwide.
        No servers, no CMS subscription, no per-page hosting cost.
      </p>

      <div class="stats-note" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        Tip: keep unique value in every row (city proof, local phone, distinct benefits) so
        programmatic pages stay useful — not thin doorway duplicates.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
